<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zeerust</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zeerust is a town in the Marico district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s North West province, near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>. It was founded in 1867 by settlers of the South African Republic on the farm of Casper Coetzee. The area was the old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahurutshe">Bahurutshe</a>, and in 1957 and 1958 it saw a revolt by Hurutshe communities against the extension of apartheid pass laws to women.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zeerust.jpg" alt="Zeerust" width="320" height="198" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ossewa · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_street_in_Zeerust.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
